        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "edde55df-9a55-5337-8bd5-74d6858b3ab0",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Cercle Proudhon\n- People: George Valois, Édouard Berth, Georges Sorel, Pierre-Joseph Proudhon\n- Works: What Is Property?\n- Places: France\n- Concepts: mutualism, federalism, property, anarchist philosophy\n\nFacts:\n- Pierre-Joseph Proudhon was born on 15 January 1809 and died on 19 January 1865.\n- Pierre-Joseph Proudhon was a French politician and the founder of mutualist philosophy.\n- Pierre-Joseph Proudhon published What Is Property? in 1840 as a nonfiction work about property and its relation to anarchist philosophy.\n- After the French Revolution of 1848, Pierre-Joseph Proudhon became a member of the French Parliament and thereafter referred to himself as a federalist.\n- Cercle Proudhon was founded in France on 16 December 1911 by George Valois and Édouard Berth.\n- Cercle Proudhon was inspired by Georges Sorel and by a selective reading of Pierre-Joseph Proudhon.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
